er project and described it as a  picture of a man in a white shirt  covered in blood with a ham hammer in  his hand and a really weird look on his  face standing on top of what looked like  an old boat they were apparently drawn  to the photo and began asking questions  like where does he come from leading  them to write 1899 like a little bit of  an experiment number five this is one  way to get an authentic score series  composer Ben Frost recorded the score  for 1899 from inside a real fishing  vessel in Iceland he would then take  these recordings and feed them through a  Bluetooth speaker to use the hull of the  ship almost like a Reverb chamber Frost  explained they were only allowed into  these fishing vessels because they were  under repair at the time so while I'm in  there with a recording of violins  there's also some guy drilling the wall  or using an arc welder in the next cabin  number six can you guess why the series  is set in 1899 well according to yantia  Frieza what we really liked about 1899  not 1898 or 1897 is that it's on a  threshold you're Crossing into a new  century stepping from something that  feels old school to something new the  future beyond that Baron also pointed  out that 1899 is very magical as he  explained it one plus eight is nine so  you have 9.99 if you turn that upside  down it's 666 the Number of the Beast  number seven imagine this on your last  day on the job Baron revealed in an  interview with tudum that on the last  day of filming all of the actors had  been put into pods and weren't able to  move going on to joke finally we could  do whatever we wanted with them odar  said that he played weird music for the  cast while Barnard recalled odar's  Antics saying and um he started playing  the Welsh national anthem Barnard added  that it made him laugh a lot number  eight did you notice all the triangles  in 1899 they are everywhere in the  show's wardrobe hidden in the background  on set and perhaps most importantly in  